  "title": "Compare standard PPO with an improved forward reference",
  "summary": "We ran standard RSL-RL PPO for 1200 updates and 3686400 transitions on 128 replicas with seed 20260914. The saved policy failed the forward, quiet and stop screens. We improved the open-loop reference and reduced forward tracking error from 0.03327 to 0.00303 m/s under the same 0.040 rad per 20 ms limiter. The improved reference passed the forward screen; it has no learned policy. We recorded contact force and motor torque at 400 Hz, preserved checkpoint and video hashes, and audited the native captures. The training process completed with exit zero; a competing COLMAP workload caused the wrapper resource check to fail. We preserved recovery state, stopped that workload under the existing authorization and completed cleanup. We integrated the RS05 direct task source from PR 22 with contact and force capture fixes; native admission remains incomplete. Stage 2 remains incomplete, and reference-assisted PPO has not run.",
